# All text files are stored AND checked out with LF line endings.
#
# Prettier enforces LF (its endOfLine default), so without this a Windows
# clone with core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF and `pnpm
# format:check` fails locally while CI (Linux, LF) passes. Pinning eol=lf
# makes every platform's working tree identical to what the tools verify.
* text=auto eol=lf
